{
  "_note": [
    "What a species asks of a player, and what their answers grant — the part of",
    "the species rules both engines implement (#112).",
    "",
    "Go resolves picks in internal/http/species.go and refuses a hero whose",
    "answers do not add up; TypeScript answers the same questions in",
    "lib/species.ts so the Forge can arm its Next button. When they disagree the",
    "player meets it as a wizard that lets them through and a forge that then",
    "says no, twenty minutes in.",
    "",
    "Only the shared contract is pinned here: is every choice answered, and what",
    "do the answers put on the sheet. Go checks more than this — unknown option,",
    "duplicate pick, a skill the background already granted — and the client",
    "deliberately does not, since the server is the authority. Asserting those",
    "would be inventing a requirement rather than recording one.",
    "",
    "skills and feats are only meaningful when complete is true; an unanswered",
    "species grants nothing, because it is not a legal hero yet."
  ],
